<ul>
<li>And here is why both matter. If preferences hold and the model runs at full scale, then one
frozen preference vector answers several policy questions with no re-estimation between them.</li>
<li>That is what a structural model buys you: reuse. Everything after the two objectives is the
first proof of it.</li>
</ul>
