<ul>
<li>Four caveats, and I want to be clear which way each one pushes.</li>
<li>The bus table is about seventeen minutes optimistic and we did not repair it. We applied only
the difference the policy makes, on top of the level the model was calibrated on. Repairing the
level means re-estimating preferences, and that is separate work.</li>
<li>The BRT's in-vehicle time is the proposal's assumption, not our measurement.</li>
<li>We value a BRT minute like a bus minute, because that is all our utility function can see. Every
real reason a BRT is nicer than a bus is missing, so this is a floor.</li>
<li>And we ran the loop once. The riders who leave their cars would relieve some congestion, and we
never collect that.</li>
<li>The last two push the same way. If anything, a fuller treatment makes this look better.</li>
</ul>
